# These files use `.venv` only

When creating or editing Python source, dependency manifests, shell or batch scripts, Makefiles, CI workflows, or container build files, follow `.cursor/rules/python-venv.mdc`.

- Shebangs, script bodies, CI steps, and docs-in-code examples invoke `.venv\Scripts\python.exe` (Windows) or `.venv/bin/python` (Unix).
- `pip install` in these files targets that interpreter: `.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pip install ...`
- Do not add a workflow, Dockerfile `RUN`, or script that installs into a system interpreter on the host.
- A container may have its own isolated Python. It still must not install packages onto the host. On the host, the interpreter remains `.venv`.
- New modules under `genesis_modules/` or `genesis/modules/` install their `requirements.txt` into the project `.venv`. Never a second environment, the user site, or system Python.
